Yech.  The RNG was really out to get me, this time.

I noticed that the nethack port on freebsd had updated to 3.4.3.  Great;
backup the log, saved games, etc.  Install, restore.

Start a character.  Hmm, a ring of slow digestion is a nice way to start
the game.

Oh, it didn't use autopickup_exceptions.  OK, edit source, reinstall.

Huh? that doesn't look like the level where I left off . . . Oh, I
didn't save the saved games again.  Oh, well; a ring of conflict isn't
such a bad starting toy . . .

A large scroll shop offered a spellbook of light and a handful of other
scrolls, and i used the blessed enchant armor for a +2 cloak.  Kitten
looted a lot for my not having any goodies for him . . .

With the ring, I headed down into the mines, leaving kitten behind at
times.  Tamed a housecat with a fortune cookie.  Stepped down into the
third mines level, and was greeted by soldier ants.  Huh?  Stragiht back
up.  Wait, that *must* be a bones level . . . 

Oh, wait.  I have a wand of lightning, and about 10 daggers.  Back down
with both cats, and engrave.  Sure enough, a double bones level, a ghost
of mine, and a ghost of my daughterrs.  Kitten died quickly, but when
the ants ran, I stepped onto the bones next to me.  A couple of scrolls
and potions, but no food.  Hmm.

Things seemed a bit tough for the cat, so we returned too the main
dungeon.  I had to pray for food again--but I did find a Eucalyptus leaf
shortly thereafter.

I was now 6th level, and hungry again.  No edible monsters.  A peaceful
pony came by, but that seemed a bit drastic.  Cat got it, anyway.

Now I'm weak, and still no food.  Once I fainted, I prayed.  Goodbye
level 6 (I don't think I've had *that* happen before . . . I know it'ss
possible, but  . . .)  . . . Oh, a newt.  That didn't do much, nor did
another little critter that came by, neither cured me of fainting.  In
desparation I ate the leaf.  Still fainting.   

Oh, good.  An orc.  Got off one attack (probably tried a force bolt, but
that would have failed, wouldn't it, making my direction an attack)
before fainting to death.

That fortune cookie and the leaf were the *only* food generated during
the game.  It wasn't even that the cat got the good corpses (except for
the pony); I just managed to go several hundred turns without seeing an
edible monster . . . (or at least one that would leave a corpse).

hawk, not so sure about 3.4.3
